        }
      ],
      "style": {
        "background": "#29241c",
        "color": "#f3e7ce",
        "borderColor": "#b99152",
        "borderWidth": 2,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 14
      },
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# The Heart of the Character\n\n## What does he want?\n\nTo discover, understand and preserve the extraordinary remnants of human history.\n\n## What does he need?\n\nTo recognize that relationships and human lives matter more than artifacts or academic achievement.\n\n## His central contradiction\n\nIndiana Jones is a rational scholar whose greatest adventures repeatedly confront him with the supernatural.\n\nHe trusts evidence, but the world keeps revealing mysteries that exceed his expectations.\n\n## His heroic flaw\n\nHis determination makes him extraordinary, but his obsession can make him careless with the people closest to him.\n\n## His defining quality\n\n**He is brave without being invulnerable.**\n\nHis victories are convincing because he suffers, fails, improvises and persists."
        },
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "cfef98fa-2f89-4b39-b69f-b2bbcfc3ba74"
